# Telegram reply format

Agent answers go to **Telegram**, not Cursor IDE. Canonical prompt wrapper: `bot/prompt.py` (`AGENT_CONTEXT` / `wrap_user_task`).

## Rules for agent replies

- **No markdown tables** (`| col | col |`) — Telegram renders them as garbage.
- Prefer plain text with clear visual spacing.
- Backlog / task lists: short header, groups `—— P0 (N) ——`, each task a block:

  ```
  FP-05  M · proposed
  Title text
  ```

  Sort P0→P3, then effort S→L; full matching list, no truncation.
- Do not rely on canvas-only deliverables; users need the text in chat.
- Keep prose short; list first when the user asked for a list.

## Bot-native backlog UI

- `/backlog` and short «дай список задач» → `bot/backlog_view.py` HTML (not the agent).
- Do not reintroduce Telegram list formatting into target-repo rules (e.g. HugSalesSolo `backlog.mdc`) — IDE keeps markdown tables.
